complexity: time=O(n log n) | space=O(n)
complexity_note: n is the length of nums.
why_time: Sorting is O(n log n), and checking the blocks is one pass.
why_space: The sorted copy and the groups hold n numbers each.
hint: `nums = sorted(nums)`.
hint: For start in `range(0, len(nums), 3)`: if `nums[start + 2] - nums[start] > k`, return `[]`.
hint: Otherwise append `nums[start:start + 3]`.
right: In sorted order, numbers that are close to each other sit side by side, so the blocks of 3 are the tightest grouping there is: if one of them is too spread out, every grouping has a group that's too spread out.
